This product includes software developed by third parties. The obligation this
file exists to satisfy is a real one and easy to overlook: a Vita `.vpk` built
with this toolchain **statically links** the Flutter engine, Skia, the Dart
runtime, ICU, HarfBuzz and their dependencies into `eboot.bin`. That makes the
`.vpk` a binary distribution of BSD-3-licensed software, and clause 2 of BSD-3
requires the copyright notice and disclaimer to travel with it — in "the
documentation and/or other materials provided with the distribution".

Shipping a `.vpk` without those materials is a licence violation regardless of
whether this repository is public.

## What to ship alongside a .vpk

`LICENSE.engine`, from the engine artifact
(`flutter-engine-vita-<version>/LICENSE.engine`).

That file is Flutter's own generated aggregate of every third-party licence in
the engine — around 30,000 lines covering Skia, Dart, ICU, HarfBuzz, libpng,
zlib, FreeType, Abseil and the rest. It is generated by upstream's licence
tooling from the engine sources, which is why it is shipped rather than
hand-written here: an inventory assembled from memory would be both incomplete
and unverifiable, and this one is neither.

It is taken from the Flutter SDK at the pinned revision — the same sources this
project builds — so it describes the components actually linked. The only delta
is this project's own patches, which are covered by [LICENSE](LICENSE).

## Nothing LGPL, since 2026-09-14

Until that date every `eboot.bin` this toolchain produced linked vitaGL and
vitaShaRK, both LGPL-3.0-or-later, and the paragraph that stood here told
whoever shipped a `.vpk` what section 4 of the LGPL asked of them. ADR-0018
found that obligation landing on every developer, ADR-0019 decided to write
the GLES2 layer here instead, and `gles2/` is that layer: BSD-3, this
project's own, over `sceGxm` and Sony's `libshacccg` on the console. No
vitaGL, no vitaShaRK, no taiHEN in the link. The history is in the two ADRs
and in git; nothing about it applies to a `.vpk` built from this tree.

## The two fonts, and what still has to be done about them

Both are under the **SIL Open Font License 1.1**, and every `.vpk` carries
both in `app0:/fonts`. An earlier version of this file called Roboto and
Roboto Mono Apache-2.0. That was wrong: `google/fonts` holds both under
`ofl/`, not `apache/`.

The OFL permits exactly what this project does. Bundling a font with software,
redistributing it, and selling the result are all allowed, and no part of the
port has to change licence because of them. Two conditions apply and one of
them we now meet:

- **The copyright notice and the licence must accompany every copy.** They now
  ship as `app0:/fonts/OFL.txt`, inside the `.vpk`. Before 2026-09-09 they did
  not, which made every `.vpk` built by this toolchain non-compliant.
- **The fonts may not be sold on their own**, and the Reserved Font Names may
  not be used on a modified version. Nothing here modifies or resells them.

**Provenance is the open item.** The Roboto copy is Flutter's unit-test
fixture: `txt/BUILD.gn` lists it under `test_fixtures("txt_fixtures")`, inside
`if (enable_unittests)`. That is why `LICENSE.engine` does not mention Roboto
at all — upstream's licence tooling excludes test fixtures, correctly, because
upstream does not ship them. We do ship it. The Roboto Mono copy came from the
DevTools bundle inside a Dart SDK prebuilt, which carries no licence file
either.

Both should be re-taken from `google/fonts` (`ofl/roboto`, `ofl/robotomono`)
with each family's own `OFL.txt` beside it. The licence is not in doubt; where
our particular binaries came from is, and a font shipped in every `.vpk`
deserves a source that ships its own licence.

## Our changes to other projects are not all BSD-3

A change to a file is a derivative work of that file, so it carries the
licence of the project it changes, not this project's. The [LICENSE](LICENSE)
at the root covers this repository's own code and does not reach them.

There are no patch files here any more. Every such change is a commit in a
fork of the project it changes, under the licence that fork already carries
([ADR-0021](docs/adr/0021-the-port-is-commits-not-patches.md)).

| Where the change lives | Licence it inherits |
|---|---|
| `flutter-vita/flutter`, `flutter-vita/dart-sdk`, `flutter-vita/skia`, `flutter-vita/zlib` | BSD-3-Clause |
| `flutter-vita/abseil-cpp` | Apache-2.0 |
| `flutter-vita/boringssl` | see BoringSSL's own `LICENSE` |
| The test-app forks (`localsend`, `keklist_flutter`, `flutter-wonderous-app`, `flutter_manga_reader`) | whatever each application uses; they are unrelated projects |

